@1 = ~I believe I do. What you are holding there is a soul coin. They are used as currency in Nine Hells and contain mortal souls bound inside the infernal iron they are made of. I can sense plenty of good souls trapped inside... and plenty of evil.~
@2 = ~Ethically speaking, releasing them would save those poor tormented souls that deserve to be in afterlife. The good ones, that is. Would you part with it so I can perform the spell on it? You've got nothing to lose.~
@3 = ~Sure. Coin is yours.~
@4 = ~I think I'd rather keep it.~
@5 = ~Nah. Let them suffer. Who cares about tormented souls.~
@6 = ~You walk a wicked path. I do not condone or approve but I am not one to forcefully seize what is now yours. Just try to think about someone other than yourself, will you? These souls are in agonising pain.~
@7 = ~Thank you. I shall perform the spell and release these wretched souls. In order to do that, I need some peace and quiet, so if you want something else, speak now.~
@8 = ~Why are you staring at that coin so much? You recognise it?~
